================================================================================
Crystal structures
================================================================================

The crystal structures in the structures folder (the Structures folder of a
release) are published third-party data. They are not part of MudLab and
neither licence above covers them. Structures from the Crystallography Open
Database (COD) are in the public domain. Structures from the American
Mineralogist Crystal Structure Database (AMCSD) may be used so long as proper
attribution is given to the journal article. README.md and CREDITS.md in that
folder give the terms and the article for every file.

================================================================================
Third-party software in the Windows release
================================================================================

The Windows release bundles Python, Qt for Python (PySide6) with the Qt
libraries, NumPy, SciPy, Matplotlib and other libraries, each under its own
licence. Qt and PySide6 are used under the GNU LGPL version 3. The notices and
the licence texts are in the release's licenses folder, starting with
licenses\THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt.
